 of the equation by 3 to isolate the variable x.\n<ul>\n<li>$\\frac{3x}{3} = \\frac{15}{3}$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Simplify both sides of the equation to find the value of x.\n<ul>\n<li>$x = 5$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Markdown\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-markdown\"># Solution\n<h2>Problem</h2>\n<p>Solve for x: 3x + 7 = 22</p>\n<h2>Answer</h2>\n<p>$$x = 5$$</p>\n<p>Simplify both sides of the equation to find the value of x.</p>\n<h2>Key Steps</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Restate the linear equation 3x + 7 = 22 and identify x as the variable to be solved.\n<ul>\n<li>$3x + 7 = 22$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Subtract 7 from both sides of the equation to isolate the term containing x.\n<ul>\n<li>$3x + 7 - 7 = 22 - 7$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Simplify both sides of the equation by performing the subtraction.\n<ul>\n<li>$3x = 15$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Divide both sides of the equation by 3 to isolate the variable x.\n<ul>\n<li>$\\frac{3x}{3} = \\frac{15}{3}$</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Simplify both sides of the equation to find the value of x.\n<ul>\n<li>$x = 5$\n</code></pre></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Hide\">\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></div>"